= Staal and the Guild-masters

The Commonwealth guild-masters and Major Guilds leaders have maintained a friendly stance toward Staal, appreciating his prioritization of their interests over those of the agrarians and his efforts to stabilize the economy. However, concerns linger over his growing state intervention and the risk that his public works campaign could trigger runaway inflation.

To address this, Staal has summoned a secret meeting with his allies and the Commonwealth’s leading guild-masters. He will offer sweeping concessions: a guarantee of capitalism’s preservation and their continued dominance over labor within a corporatist framework. In return, they are expected to pool their resources for unrestricted use by the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span>.

- @schleicher_2: The <span style="color: #C0A054;">guild-masters</span> are granted their place in the new order.

@schleicher_2
on-arrival: {!
Q.industrialists_gnu = 1

Q.pro_republic -= 3;

Q.commons_staal

Q.commons_gnu -= 4;
Q.burgher_gnu += 10;
Q.guild_gnu += 10;
Q.landed_gnu += 4;
Q.disfavored_gnu -= 4;

Q.gnu_relation -= 10;
!}

Staal continues to walk a tightrope between appeasing organized labor and retaining the favor of the Commonwealth’s industrial elite. Nonetheless, the <span style="color: #BFC8CC;">**GNU**</span> secures over five million crowns in funding from a consortium of Commonwealth businesses—chiefly those tied to rearmament, who see Staal’s survival as essential to their own profits.